slug: osce-viva-technique
title: Passing the OSCE and Viva — A Method, Not Luck
area: Exam & Career
level: Foundation
best: 2nd year onwards
minutes: 12
hook: OSCE and viva exams reward a clear routine under time pressure. Learn how stations are marked, a simple structure for every station and how to practise so that you stay calm. || OSCE aur viva exams waqt ke dabao mein saaf routine ko inaam dete hain. Seekhein stations kaise marks hote hain, har station ke liye saada dhancha aur practice kaise karein taake aap pur-sukoon rahein.
goal: By the end, you'll read a station task quickly, follow a safe routine (introduce, consent, expose, examine, explain), manage the clock, and practise with a partner using a checklist. || End tak aap station ka task jaldi parhenge, mehfooz routine (taaruf, razamandi, expose, examine, explain) par chalenge, ghari sambhalenge, aur partner ke saath checklist se practice karenge.

say: An **OSCE** (objective structured clinical examination) moves you through short stations. At each one, an examiner marks you on a **checklist**: they look for specific actions, not for brilliance. Marks come from **communication and safety** as much as from technique. A **viva** is a spoken exam where you explain your reasoning aloud. In both, a **clear structure** gets marks even when you feel nervous. || **OSCE** (objective structured clinical examination) aap ko chhote stations se guzarta hai. Har station par examiner **checklist** par marks deta hai: woh khaas amal dekhte hain, shandaar pan nahi. Marks technique ke saath **communication aur hifazat** se bhi aate hain. **Viva** zubani imtihan hai jis mein aap apni reasoning bol kar samjhate hain. Dono mein **saaf dhancha** ghabrahat mein bhi marks dilata hai.
analogy: Think of an OSCE as a **driving test**. The examiner is not looking for a racing driver but for mirrors, signals and safe habits every time. If you do the safe basics in the same order at every station, you collect the easy marks, and you have your mind free for the hard part. || OSCE ko **driving test** samjhein. Examiner race driver nahi dhoondta balkay har baar mirrors, signals aur mehfooz aadatein dekhta hai. Agar aap har station par mehfooz buniyadi kaam ek hi tarteeb mein karein to aasan marks mil jate hain, aur mushkil hissay ke liye dimagh azad rehta hai.
steps: A routine for every station || Har station ke liye routine
step: Read the task and plan :: Use the reading time to underline the task, the patient and the time. Decide your first three actions before you walk in. || Task parhein aur plan banayein :: Parhne ke waqt mein task, mareez aur waqt par line lagayein. Andar jane se pehle apne pehle teen kaam tay karein.
step: Introduce and get consent :: Wash your hands, say your name and role, check the patient's name, explain what you will do and ask permission. These are almost always marked. || Taaruf aur razamandi :: Hath dhoyein, apna naam aur kirdar batayein, mareez ka naam check karein, batayein ke kya karenge aur ijazat maangein. Yeh lagbhag hamesha marks hote hain.
step: Do the task in order :: Position and expose the patient respectfully, look first, then ask about pain, then examine the unaffected side before the affected side, and keep checking comfort. || Task tarteeb se karein :: Mareez ko izzat se position aur expose karein, pehle dekhein, phir dard poochhein, phir mutasir side se pehle sehatmand side examine karein, aur aaram check karte rahein.
step: Explain and close :: Tell the patient what you found in simple words, say what happens next, ask if they have questions and thank them. Keep an eye on the clock. || Samjhayein aur khatam karein :: Mareez ko saade alfaz mein batayein kya paya, aage kya hoga, sawal poochhein aur shukriya ada karein. Ghari par nazar rakhein.

check: Which action is almost always on the OSCE checklist? || Kaun sa amal OSCE checklist mein lagbhag hamesha hota hai?
ok: Introducing yourself, washing hands and gaining consent || Taaruf, hath dhona aur razamandi lena || Yes — these safety and communication marks are easy to collect. || Haan — hifazat aur communication ke yeh marks aasan hain.
no: Performing the test as fast as possible || Test jitna tez ho sake karna || Speed is not marked and can cause errors. || Raftar ke marks nahi aur ghalti ho sakti hai.
no: Skipping the explanation to save time || Waqt bachane ke liye wazahat chhor dena || Explaining to the patient is usually marked. || Mareez ko samjhana aam taur par marks hota hai.
compare: OSCE or viva? || OSCE ya viva?
head: Feature || Khasiyat ;; OSCE || OSCE ;; Viva || Viva
row: What you do || Aap kya karte hain ;; Perform a task on a patient or model || Mareez ya model par task karte hain ;; Answer questions aloud || Zubani sawalon ke jawab dete hain
row: How it is marked || Marks kaise ;; A checklist of actions and communication || Amal aur communication ki checklist ;; Quality of reasoning and safety || Reasoning aur hifazat ka maiyar
row: Best preparation || Behtareen tayyari ;; Rehearse with a partner and a stopwatch || Partner aur stopwatch ke saath mashq ;; Explain topics aloud to a friend || Dost ko topics bol kar samjhana
row: Common error || Aam ghalti ;; Forgetting consent, exposure or the closing explanation || Razamandi, expose ya akhri wazahat bhoolna ;; Giving a list of facts without a reason || Wajah ke baghair haqaiq ki fehrist dena
memory: **Same routine, every station.** Introduce, consent, expose, examine, explain. A routine you have rehearsed frees your mind for the unusual part. || **Har station par wohi routine.** Taaruf, razamandi, expose, examine, wazahat. Mashq ki hui routine aap ke dimagh ko ghair mamooli hissay ke liye azad karti hai.
mistake: **Freezing when you forget a step.** Examiners do not mark silence as failure; they mark safety. If you forget something, say "I would also check..." and continue. Never invent a finding. || **Ek qadam bhool kar jam jana.** Examiners khamoshi ko nakami nahi, hifazat ko marks dete hain. Kuch bhool jayein to kahein "Main yeh bhi check karunga..." aur aage barhein. Kabhi finding gharh kar na batayein.
check: You realise you forgot to ask about allergies halfway through the station. What should you do? || Station ke darmiyan yaad aaya ke allergies poochhna bhool gaye. Kya karein?
ok: Pause politely, ask now and carry on || Narmi se ruk kar abhi poochhein aur jaari rakhein || Yes — safety questions asked late still earn credit, and silence does not. || Haan — hifazat ke sawal der se poochhna bhi marks deta hai, khamoshi nahi.
no: Pretend you asked earlier || Aise zahir karein ke pehle poochha tha || Honesty matters and examiners notice. || Imandari ahem hai aur examiners dekh lete hain.
no: Leave it out to avoid looking unsure || Anjaan lagne se bachne ke liye chhor dein || Missing a safety step costs marks. || Hifazat ka qadam chhorna marks kata deta hai.
check: How should you practise for the exam? || Imtihan ki tayyari kaise karein?
ok: Rehearse stations aloud with a partner, a stopwatch and the checklist || Partner, stopwatch aur checklist ke saath stations bol kar dohrayein || Yes — realistic practice and feedback improve performance fastest. || Haan — haqeeqi mashq aur feedback karkardagi sab se tez behtar karte hain.
no: Read the textbook only, silently || Sirf khamoshi se kitaab parhein || Passive reading does not train performance. || Passive parhna karkardagi train nahi karta.
no: Practise only the techniques you enjoy || Sirf pasandeeda techniques practise karein || Exams test the whole range. || Imtihan poori range parakhte hain.
clinic: **Use the Virtual Patient and Skills Lab as stations.** Pick a case, set a ten-minute timer and talk through your routine aloud. Then ask a friend to mark you on the checklist and note one thing to improve. Three short practices a week beat one long one the night before. || **Virtual Patient aur Skills Lab ko stations ki tarah istemal karein.** Ek case chunein, das minute ka timer lagayein aur apni routine bol kar chalayein. Phir dost se checklist par marks karwayein aur ek behtari ka nukta likhein. Haftay mein teen chhoti mashqein ek raat pehle ki lambi mashq se behtar hain.
reveal: Why do examiners reward a clear structure even when the technique is imperfect? || Examiners technique kamzor hone par bhi saaf dhanche ko inaam kyun dete hain? || A structure shows safe habits that carry over to real patients: consent, privacy, comparison, communication and escalation. Technique improves with practice, but unsafe or disorganised habits are much harder to correct, so checklists reward them heavily. || Dhancha mehfooz aadatein dikhata hai jo haqeeqi mareezon par bhi chalti hain: razamandi, parda, muqabla, communication aur escalation. Technique mashq se behtar hota hai, magar ghair mehfooz ya be-tarteeb aadatein theek karna bohat mushkil hai, is liye checklists inhein bohat ahmiyat deti hain.
case: In a shoulder station you forget to ask about pain before moving the arm, then realise it with 4 minutes left. You are nervous and want to skip ahead to the special tests. || A missed safety step is recoverable if you act on it honestly; skipping the explanation would lose more marks. || Say you would like to ask about pain now, do so, then continue with the same routine and finish with an explanation. || You collect the safety marks late and complete the station in time.
safety: **In real clinical exams, never invent findings or examine without consent.** If a station asks you to do something unsafe, say what you would do and why, and refer or stop. Patient safety, dignity and honesty are marked more than any technique. Look after your own health: sleep, eat and take breaks before an exam day. || **Haqeeqi clinical imtihanon mein kabhi findings gharh kar na batayein aur razamandi ke baghair examine na karein.** Agar station koi ghair mehfooz kaam kahe to batayein aap kya karte aur kyun, aur refer ya ruk jayein. Mareez ki hifazat, izzat aur imandari kisi bhi technique se zyada marks hoti hain. Imtihan se pehle neend, khana aur break se apni sehat ka khayal rakhein.
summary: OSCE stations are marked on checklists of actions, communication and safety, so a routine earns reliable marks. || OSCE stations amal, communication aur hifazat ki checklist par marks hote hain, is liye routine bharosemand marks dilati hai.
summary: Use the same routine at every station: read, introduce, consent, expose, examine, explain, and watch the clock. || Har station par wohi routine: parhein, taaruf, razamandi, expose, examine, wazahat, aur ghari dekhein.
summary: If you forget a step, say so and carry on; practise aloud with a partner, a stopwatch and a checklist. || Koi qadam bhool jayein to batayein aur jaari rakhein; partner, stopwatch aur checklist ke saath bol kar mashq karein.
card: What is an OSCE? || OSCE kya hai? || An objective structured clinical examination of short, marked stations. || Chhote, marks hone wale stations ka objective structured clinical examination.
card: Name the five parts of the routine. || Routine ke paanch hissay batayein. || Introduce, consent, expose, examine, explain. || Taaruf, razamandi, expose, examine, wazahat.
card: What should you do if you forget a step? || Koi qadam bhool jayein to kya karein? || Say so, do it now and continue. || Batayein, abhi karein aur jaari rakhein.
card: How should you practise? || Mashq kaise karein? || Aloud, with a partner, a stopwatch and a checklist. || Bol kar, partner, stopwatch aur checklist ke saath.
deeper: Virtual Patient || /virtual-patient || Practise full history, examination and diagnosis stations. || Mukammal history, examination aur diagnosis stations ki mashq karein.
deeper: Clinical reasoning lesson || /learn/clinical-reasoning-thinking-errors || Structure your thinking for the viva. || Viva ke liye apni soch ko dhancha dein.
source: Harden RM, Stevenson M, Downie WW, Wilson GM. Assessment of clinical competence using objective structured examination. BMJ 1975;1:447-451. || assessment clinical competence objective structured examination
source: Khan KZ, Ramachandran S, Gaunt K, Pushkar P. The Objective Structured Clinical Examination (OSCE): AMEE Guide No. 81. Part I: an historical and theoretical perspective. Med Teach 2013;35:e1437-e1446. || OSCE AMEE guide historical theoretical perspective
